course: dictionary
lesson: 6519
title: Neon: a gas and a bright colour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word neon has two jobs. It is the name of a gas, and it is also a describing word for very bright colours. Context tells you which one is meant. «Neon gas glows orange-red when electricity passes through it» is about the gas, because the sentence talks about electricity and glowing.
explain: When neon comes before a colour, like neon green or neon pink, it describes something very bright and glowing, such as a vest or a sign. Ask yourself: is this talking about a substance, or about how bright something looks? The words around it give the clue.
explain: Try the swap check. In «Tropical fish such as angelfish and neon tetras need warm water», a neon tetra is a kind of fish, and the sentence tells you what it needs: warm water. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Neon» is a gas that has no colour or smell in ordinary air, but it glows bright red-orange when electricity passes through it.
fact: Neon lights are bright glowing tubes used in shop signs.
fact: As an adjective, «neon» describes very bright, glowing colours, like neon green.
fact: In science, neon is a chemical element with the symbol Ne and the number 10 on the periodic table. It is a noble gas, which means it does not react easily.
fact: «Neon gas glows orange-red when electricity passes through it; each element glows with its own colours.»
exercise: «Neon gas glows orange-red when electricity passes through it.» What is neon in this sentence? | A kind of paint | A loud noise | A type of fish | *A gas that glows when electricity passes through it
exercise: Mia says «a neon vest keeps you safe on a bike». What does neon mean in «neon vest»? | *Very bright, glowing colour | Made of metal | Soft and quiet
exercise: In «neon tetras need warm water», what do neon tetras need? | Cool water | Salt water | *Warm water | Ice
test: Sam sees a shop sign that glows red and says, «The neon is bright tonight.» What does neon most likely mean here? | Warm water for fish | A quiet whisper | *Glowing tube lights used in signs | A kind of bread
test: Which of these is the correct chemical symbol for neon, and where is it on the periodic table? | A liquid that is cold | Symbol N, number 1 | A metal that rusts | *Symbol Ne, number 10
exam: Which statement about neon is true? | Neon is always a cool blue | Neon is only a colour and never a gas | Neon is a kind of food | *Neon is a noble gas that does not react easily
